<main><section class="page-hero section-shell"><span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span><h1>Common questions, answered clearly.</h1><p>If something is not covered here, the source documentation and repository are the best references.</p></section>
<section class="section-shell section"><div class="faq-list"><?php $faqs=[['What is NotYVOS?','A development-stage x86-64 operating system with a native kernel, desktop environment, persistent storage, hardware drivers and a PS3 runtime foundation.'],['Is NotYVOS a Linux distribution?','No. It is a freestanding operating-system project with its own kernel and userland components.'],['What hardware does it target?','The primary architecture is x86-64. Current work includes framebuffer/VBE, ACPI, AHCI, Intel e1000, HDA, PS/2 and USB foundations.'],['Can it run Windows .exe files?','No. Windows PE and Win32 compatibility are explicitly excluded from the current roadmap.'],['Does it include PS3 firmware?','No. User-supplied PS3 firmware is isolated to the PS3 runtime domain and is not redistributed by the project.'],['What comes next?','The active milestone is init-program debugging. Queued work includes GameRunner integration, production networking, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, NYFS maturity, firewall work and NotYVFirm.'],['How can I learn the architecture?','Start with the Architecture page here, then read docs/architecture.md, docs/data flow.md and docs/roadmap.md in the main repository.'],['Who develops NotYVOS?','The project is developed by NotY215. See the Developer page for project links and contact points.']];foreach($faqs as [$q,$a]): ?><details class="faq-item"><summary><?= htmlspecialchars($q) ?><span>+</span></summary><p><?= htmlspecialchars($a) ?></p></details><?php endforeach; ?></div></section></main><?php require __DIR__.'/includes/footer.php'; ?>